  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Extent to which manufacturers have the capacities to produce Ozone friendly appliances/products
Scale: 
1. Capacity building of stakeholders to limited extent (1-25%)
2. Capacity building of stakeholders to reasonable extent (26-50%)
3. Capacity building of stakeholders to large extent (51-100%)

1.2: Extent to which policy regulation/guidelines at the federal and provincial level exist to ensure introduction of usage of clean technology for the protection of ozone layer

Scale: 
1. No policy regulation/guidelines both at the federal and provincial level exist (0%)
2. policy regulation/guidelines at  provincial level exist (1-50%); 
  [Desc.: If two provinces then 25% and if four provinces then 50%]
3. policy regulation/guidelines at both federal and provincial level (51-100%)

1.3: Number of eligible importers/manufacturers receive allocated quota to import Ozone Depleting Substances (ODS) 

1.4: Number of import data reports, generated by FBR reviewed and compiled by National Ozone Unit, are submitted to MLF</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline 1.1: Scale item 2
Baseline 1.2: Scale item 2
Baseline 1.3: 26 [21 are total quota holders who are allocated quota on yearly basis]
Baseline 1.4: 2</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 3 [Maximum industry and end users will be aware of the advantages of new technology and its impact towards Ozone protection and climate mitigation]
1.2: Scale 3 [51-100% policy regulation/guidelines at both federal and provincial level exist]
1.3: 26 [Quota to 26 eligible HCFC quota holder was allocated on yearly basis]
1.4: 2 [2 Import data reports analyzed to ensure compliance to Montreal Protocol]</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 2 [industry and end users are well aware of the advantages of new technology and its impact towards Ozone protection and climate mitigation. CFCs has been totally eliminated while the HCFCs based industries are being covered to HFCs and / or HCs to protect the fragile ozone layer]
1.2: Scale 2 [2. policy regulation/guidelines at provincial level exist (1-50%); (Desc.: If two provinces then 25% and if four provinces then 50%)]
1.3: 21 [Quota to 21 eligible HCFC quota holder was allocated on yearly basis]
1.4: 12 [12 Import data reports analyzed to ensure compliance to Montreal Protocol. 2 reports i.e. A7 Data Report and Country Programme Reports are submitted to MLFS and Ozone Secretariat to remain in compliance with regard to the provisions of the Montreal Protocol]</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 3 No target
1.2: Scale 3 [policy regulation/guidelines at both federal and provincial level (51-100%)]
1.3: 26   [21 are total quota holders who are allocated quota on yearly basis]
1.4: 2   [2 Import data reports to be thoroughly analyzed to ensure compliance to the Montreal Protocol]</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 3 No result
1.2: Scale 3 [no progress]
1.3: 26     [no progress]
1.4: 2      [no progress]

Note: Submission on update of Article 07 by National Ozone Unit. Due to change in implementation modality, the project team was laid off with request of recruitment of new team through UNDP. The recruitment process is in final stages.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
